  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Decentralisering Liberia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Liberia Decentralization Support Program - Decentralisation Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Deconcentrated functions and corresponding resources managed at the assigned level of government implemented;
2) Service delivery and accountability of local governments is improved;
3) Legal and regulatory framework for decentralization is in place;
4) MIA is capacitated to lead and implement decentralization reforms.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det liberianska inrikesministeriet har ans&#xf6;kt om bidrag till finansiering av Liberia Decentralization Support Program (LDSP), under 2016-2017. Programmet har f&#xf6;ljande f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade (outcome) resultat:  Den statliga administrationen p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5; lokal f&#xf6;rvaltar de delegerade resurserna och levererar offentliga tj&#xe4;nster; den lokala f&#xf6;rvaltningens leverans av tj&#xe4;nster och ansvarstagande har f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrats; det legala ramverket f&#xf6;r decentraliserad stryre &#xe4;r f&#xe4;rdig; det liberianska inrikesministeriet och Governance Commission har &#xf6;kad kapacitet att leda och genomf&#xf6;ra decentraliseringsreformer. 
Insatsens totala budget &#xe4;r upskattad till USD 19.9 miljoner, och budgeten f&#xf6;r 2016-2017 &#xe4;r USD 12.7 miljoner. Sverige planerar att bidra med SEK 45 miljoner. &#xd6;vriga finansi&#xe4;rer &#xe4;r den liberianska staten och utvecklingspartners EU, UNDP, UNMIL och USAID.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Liberian Ministry of Internal Affairs has requested Embassy of Sweden support for funding Liberia Decentralization Support Program during 2015-2017.  
The expected outcomes are: &quot;Deconcentrated services and corresponding resources management at the assigned level of government; improved service delivery and accountability of local governments; necessary legal and regulatory framework for decentralization is in place; and capacity-building of the responsible institutions. 
The intervention&apos;s total budget is USD 19.9 million. The other development partners contributing with funding  EU USD 5.5 million, UNDP USD 2.5 million, USAID USD 1.0 million and UNMIL USD 0.5 million. The Liberian government has allocated in the current annual budget USD 0.5 million. Sweden will contribute USD 5.2 million.</narrative>
  </description>
